00:22:34.630 --> 00:22:35.750
Well, that's Steve, right?

539
00:22:35.750 --> 00:22:39.590
I mean, he got everything scripted, but sometimes he would zhuzh in the moment.

540
00:22:39.930 --> 00:22:41.530
Here's what it said in the script.

541
00:22:42.010 --> 00:22:42.950
Oh, God.

542
00:22:43.090 --> 00:22:43.870
It's happening.

543
00:22:44.150 --> 00:22:44.930
Let me through.

544
00:22:45.150 --> 00:22:45.870
Let me through.

545
00:22:46.170 --> 00:22:46.990
Stay calm.

546
00:22:47.210 --> 00:22:47.850
Stay calm.

547
00:22:48.030 --> 00:22:49.490
Stay effing calm.

548
00:22:49.910 --> 00:22:53.930
And then Michael violently pushes his way through to the front.

549
00:22:54.870 --> 00:22:56.410
I think we did it.

550
00:22:56.410 --> 00:22:58.570
I mean, very accurately.

551
00:22:58.890 --> 00:23:00.590
We have more fan questions.

552
00:23:00.750 --> 00:23:01.910
Angela, Jaden C.

553
00:23:02.070 --> 00:23:06.650
wants to know, how many times did Michael throw the projector into the window?

554
00:23:07.010 --> 00:23:09.090
Well, he starts with the chair, right?

555
00:23:09.570 --> 00:23:10.490
That's right.

556
00:23:10.490 --> 00:23:12.030
It does not break.

557
00:23:12.390 --> 00:23:17.210
And Randy said that for that, we used a plane of plexiglass.

558
00:23:17.490 --> 00:23:18.790
Because they didn't want it to break.

559
00:23:18.950 --> 00:23:20.930
They wanted his first attempt not to go well.

560
00:23:21.070 --> 00:23:21.610
Yes.

561
00:23:22.230 --> 00:23:29.330
Then they replaced the plexiglass with breakaway glass, and it shatters very realistically,

562
00:23:29.730 --> 00:23:32.590
but it never shatters in a sharp or dangerous way.

563
00:23:32.870 --> 00:23:34.650
I have a little fun fact for you.

564
00:23:34.950 --> 00:23:40.030
In the olden days of Hollywood, this was known as candy glass.

565
00:23:40.370 --> 00:23:45.730
I know that, Jenna, because I got a tour of an old Western set with my dad, and they

566
00:23:45.730 --> 00:23:50.730
were like, all those windows that guys get thrown out the bars in and the saloon, that

567
00:23:50.730 --> 00:23:51.530
was candy.

568
00:23:51.890 --> 00:23:52.410
Candy!

569
00:23:52.750 --> 00:23:52.990
Yeah.

570
00:23:52.990 --> 00:23:53.710
You could eat it!

571
00:23:53.950 --> 00:23:58.850
I guess nowadays, they don't make it out of candy, but Randy said old schoolers still

572
00:23:58.850 --> 00:24:02.230
call it candy glass, even though now it's called breakaway glass.

573
00:24:02.450 --> 00:24:02.650
Okay.

574
00:24:03.070 --> 00:24:07.910
And Randy also told us, Jaden, in answer to your question, they got it in one take.

575
00:24:08.330 --> 00:24:11.590
One throw of the projector broke the breakaway glass.

576
00:24:11.810 --> 00:24:12.610
There you go.

577
00:24:13.310 --> 00:24:18.290
Jaden would also like to know, how many times did Kevin break the vending machine?

578
00:24:18.290 --> 00:24:20.610
I reached out to Brian Baumgartner.

579
00:24:20.770 --> 00:24:23.930
He said he thought it took about two to three takes.

