00:24:47.190 --> 00:24:48.870
I can't believe no one wrote in about it.

590
00:24:48.970 --> 00:24:52.890
I know exactly the moment you're talking about because it was such a big deal to all

591
00:24:52.890 --> 00:24:53.790
of us on set.

592
00:24:53.910 --> 00:24:58.990
And maybe people don't realize that because of what a badass Chris Workman is.

593
00:24:59.170 --> 00:25:05.550
So what we're talking about is the moment when, led by Kevin, the Dunder Mifflin employees

594
00:25:05.550 --> 00:25:11.530
are running through the kitchen and take down our camera operator, Randall Einhorn.

595
00:25:11.530 --> 00:25:14.070
Guys, this was a total mistake.

596
00:25:14.430 --> 00:25:14.910
Yeah.

597
00:25:15.130 --> 00:25:17.870
We were like, oh my God, Randall's down.

598
00:25:18.150 --> 00:25:19.570
But only for a few seconds.

599
00:25:19.990 --> 00:25:24.510
We reached out to Randall because we had to hear this story from his perspective.

600
00:25:24.610 --> 00:25:26.510
When Brian mowed him down.

601
00:25:27.010 --> 00:25:32.370
I remember when I was running backwards through the break room and Brian Baumgartner, who plays

602
00:25:32.370 --> 00:25:35.730
Kevin, was running at me because he's frantically trying to get out of there.

603
00:25:35.730 --> 00:25:40.930
And he, he just kept running on me, running and gaining on me and gaining on me.

604
00:25:40.990 --> 00:25:44.890
And I'm running backwards with the camera and he just got so close that I think he hit

605
00:25:44.890 --> 00:25:46.670
me and I, I, and I hit the ground.

606
00:25:46.910 --> 00:25:53.110
I went down, but my camera says Chris Workman, who's really strong guy, just caught me with

607
00:25:53.110 --> 00:25:57.430
one arm, caught me and the camera with one arm and put me back on my feet.

608
00:25:57.550 --> 00:25:59.630
And I'm like a 200 pound guy.

609
00:25:59.750 --> 00:26:01.390
The camera's nearly 40 pounds.

610
00:26:01.610 --> 00:26:03.090
And Chris just lifted me up.

611
00:26:03.090 --> 00:26:08.070
I didn't even know if I hit the ground, it was, but that, that shot of me going down

612
00:26:08.070 --> 00:26:09.930
and getting back up actually made the show.

613
00:26:10.150 --> 00:26:12.130
So thank you, Chris Workman for picking me up.

614
00:26:12.230 --> 00:26:15.650
And thank you, Brian Baumgartner for running into me and making such a cool shot.

615
00:26:17.850 --> 00:26:23.110
Well, Angela, I felt like we also needed to hear from Brian Baumgartner about this moment,

616
00:26:23.610 --> 00:26:24.990
the mower and the mode.

617
00:26:25.410 --> 00:26:25.850
Exactly.

618
00:26:26.230 --> 00:26:27.890
We needed a point counterpoint.

619
00:26:28.750 --> 00:26:30.970
Well, thank you, Randall.

620
00:26:30.970 --> 00:26:35.370
You know, I, you know, I wanted to make fun of you for getting the story wrong, but, but

621
00:26:35.370 --> 00:26:38.330
you complimented me and got the story a hundred percent, right?

622
00:26:38.510 --> 00:26:41.270
I mean, look, I had people running behind me.

623
00:26:41.470 --> 00:26:41.910
Okay.

624
00:26:41.910 --> 00:26:47.650
So I, I, I, I had to run over whatever was in front of me or I would have gotten run over

625
00:26:47.650 --> 00:26:48.210
myself.

626
00:26:48.670 --> 00:26:54.410
Um, but actually come to think of it, it's the first time that anyone has ever told me that

627
00:26:54.410 --> 00:26:55.990
I, I've outrun anyone.

628
00:26:56.370 --> 00:26:59.970
I mean, you, you were running backwards, carrying a camera.

629
00:27:00.270 --> 00:27:06.810
Uh, but yeah, I, I had to, to, to put you down and look, the thing I remember is yes,

630
00:27:06.990 --> 00:27:09.430
you, you went all the way to your back as I recall.

631
00:27:09.630 --> 00:27:15.710
And for me out of the corner of my eye, it looked like Chris Workman, one hand picked you

632
00:27:15.710 --> 00:27:16.930
up, put you back on the feet.

633
00:27:16.930 --> 00:27:22.050
And like the pro, uh, that you are, well, you, you just kept filming.

634
00:27:22.310 --> 00:27:24.870
I'm so happy that it made it into the cut.

635
00:27:24.870 --> 00:27:26.810
And it's, it's one of my favorite episodes.

636
00:27:27.010 --> 00:27:29.050
It, it aired after the Superbowl, obviously.

637
00:27:29.470 --> 00:27:31.910
And, and that was a big deal for me.

638
00:27:32.130 --> 00:27:35.570
And, um, and yeah, one of our funniest cold opens for sure.

639
00:27:35.910 --> 00:27:41.190
Well, lady, I just remember that moment so vividly because I do remember Randall is

640
00:27:41.190 --> 00:27:41.570
down.

641
00:27:41.770 --> 00:27:42.450
What do we do?

642
00:27:42.670 --> 00:27:43.710
And then Randall is up.

643
00:27:43.830 --> 00:27:45.150
I guess we continue.

644
00:27:45.150 --> 00:27:48.360
You, amazing to me.

645
00:27:48.520 --> 00:27:50.360
And that's the only time it happened.

646
00:27:50.360 --> 00:27:52.040
And that's the take we used.

647
00:27:52.420 --> 00:27:53.520
Chris Workman, man.

648
00:27:54.000 --> 00:27:55.300
He is a machine.

649
00:27:56.420 --> 00:27:57.060
All right.

