00:28:34.640 --> 00:28:35.460
I was there.

666
00:28:36.120 --> 00:28:38.860
But the cat didn't work those moments.

667
00:28:38.860 --> 00:28:39.260
Okay.

668
00:28:39.940 --> 00:28:40.160
Yeah.

669
00:28:40.160 --> 00:28:46.400
The cat did have to work one moment, Jenna, with all of us, where I open the drawer and

670
00:28:46.400 --> 00:28:47.020
you reveal.

671
00:28:47.340 --> 00:28:47.660
Yeah.

672
00:28:47.880 --> 00:28:49.900
You guys are all in the background for that moment.

673
00:28:50.300 --> 00:28:55.840
And I had to actually pick the cat up and walk over to where I would have tossed it.

674
00:28:55.980 --> 00:28:56.680
And that was it.

675
00:28:56.800 --> 00:28:59.580
That's all I had to do with the cat, with the group there.

676
00:29:00.240 --> 00:29:01.640
Jenna, this cat was massive.

677
00:29:01.980 --> 00:29:03.120
It looks big.

678
00:29:03.120 --> 00:29:05.180
I'm like, did you cast the biggest cat they had?

679
00:29:05.280 --> 00:29:07.960
Did you see the big one in the corner and say, we want that, dude?

680
00:29:08.900 --> 00:29:14.340
Just taking it out of the drawer with the chaos, not even doing anything with it, just picking

681
00:29:14.340 --> 00:29:16.220
it up and taking it to my spot.

682
00:29:16.820 --> 00:29:18.940
The cat was like, I'm out of here.

683
00:29:19.980 --> 00:29:25.740
So I was really glad when we actually filmed the stunt part that you guys were all gone.

684
00:29:26.440 --> 00:29:26.840
Right.

685
00:29:27.180 --> 00:29:28.060
Oh, my gosh.

686
00:29:28.200 --> 00:29:30.520
Less activity for the cat to deal with.

687
00:29:30.620 --> 00:29:32.660
The cat was already like, where am I?

688
00:29:32.700 --> 00:29:33.340
What's going on?

689
00:29:33.660 --> 00:29:34.160
All right.

690
00:29:34.280 --> 00:29:36.180
So a lot of things went in to make this happen.

