1327
00:58:48.720 --> 00:58:49.120
Okay.

1328
00:58:49.260 --> 00:58:53.300
In January of 2019, Rolling Stones ran this story.

1329
00:58:53.840 --> 00:59:02.560
A scene from the office that dealt with first aid technique is credited to helping save a life after an Arizona man, despite having no CPR training,

1330
00:59:03.120 --> 00:59:05.620
managed to resuscitate a woman in medical distress.

1331
00:59:05.920 --> 00:59:09.480
His name, interestingly enough, is Cross Scott.

1332
00:59:09.800 --> 00:59:10.220
Whoa.

1333
00:59:10.400 --> 00:59:10.560
Yeah.

1334
00:59:10.780 --> 00:59:11.620
His last name is Scott.

1335
00:59:12.000 --> 00:59:17.940
So he found an unconscious woman behind the wheel of her car that was rolling down a dirt road.

1336
00:59:18.160 --> 00:59:18.640
Wow.

1337
00:59:18.720 --> 00:59:21.920
He smashed the window, got her out.

1338
00:59:22.420 --> 00:59:26.720
And then he's quoted as saying, I've never prepared myself for CPR in my life.

1339
00:59:26.840 --> 00:59:28.240
I had no idea what I was doing.

1340
00:59:29.520 --> 00:59:36.620
Thankfully, Scott had seen the episode of the office that dealt with CPR training and knew to do chest compressions to the cadence of staying alive.

1341
00:59:36.620 --> 00:59:46.480
They reached out to Courtney Slanaker, executive director of the Red Cross Southern Arizona chapter, and she told the Daily Star that if you don't do CPR, the victim will die.

1342
00:59:46.480 --> 00:59:47.720
Don't be afraid to act.

1343
00:59:47.880 --> 00:59:51.380
Whatever you do will help that victim and hopefully prevent a death.

1344
00:59:51.520 --> 00:59:58.240
And Courtney confirmed that staying alive is, in fact, the correct rhythm for chest compressions.

1345
00:59:58.580 --> 00:59:59.120
Wow.

1346
00:59:59.380 --> 01:00:01.380
Jen Salata, you got it right.

1347
01:00:02.820 --> 01:00:13.920
There's so many, guys, but just recently in January of this year, the Today Show shared a story about a four-year-old girl who collapsed while playing tag, and her dad, Matt Uber,

1348
01:00:14.620 --> 01:00:19.660
