1349
01:00:19.660 --> 01:00:24.140
And he's quoted as saying, when I was trying to think about what to do about CPR,

1350
01:00:24.580 --> 01:00:31.640
my mind literally went to that episode of the office where they are doing CPR training and doing the compressions to the beat of staying alive.

1351
01:00:31.900 --> 01:00:35.940
I mean, that just got me choked up to imagine that father in that moment.

1352
01:00:35.940 --> 01:00:36.620
I know.

1353
01:00:36.620 --> 01:00:39.360
And then he had something, anything he could do.

1354
01:00:39.560 --> 01:00:40.340
I know.

1355
01:00:41.340 --> 01:00:42.040
I know.

1356
01:00:42.120 --> 01:00:42.720
And there's more.

1357
01:00:42.920 --> 01:00:46.340
I know there's more stories, but those two were two that stood out to me.

1358
01:00:46.800 --> 01:00:47.280
Amazing.

